Z||000000||JetroGT||02-07-2000||02:18 PM||||Is their any difference between the V6 cradels and the 4cyl cradels?  Different mounting holes for engine mounts and such?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||02-07-2000||02:39 PM||||not really. in 86.5 a anchor point was added for the altered automatic trany mount, but other wise all pre88 cradles are the same. Car makers like to use the same part in as many things as posible. Having a uneversal cradle is cheaper than having diferant ones. Makes assembly screwups harded as well. If you only have one part you don't have to think about which part to pick up next.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||02-07-2000||07:41 PM||||Are you saying that all cradles are the same irregardless of the intended motor?  What about '84 since they hadn't had a V6 yet?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodrv6||02-07-2000||10:49 PM||||I don't know if the motor mount holes are different on 84 cradles, but the mounts for the inner end of the rear tie rods are unique on the 84's.  In 85 GM lowered these mount holes by 5mm in an attempt to improve the rear suspension geometry.  They were trying to reduce or eliminate the "bumpsteering" at the rear. (Bumpsteering is the change in rear toe-in due to the vertical travel of the suspension.)||||reg||4
